<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:course xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="GWS 202" href="schedule/2022/spring/GWS/202.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2022" href="schedule/2022.xml">2022</calendarYear><term id="120221" href="schedule/2022/spring.xml">Spring 2022</term><subject id="GWS" href="schedule/2022/spring/GWS.xml">Gender and Women's Studies</subject></parents><label>Sexualities</label><description>Surveys sexualities from multiple perspectives, standpoints, disciplines, and theories. How have different cultures, different people, and different viewpoints understood, shaped, and interpreted sex, sexualities and genders? Course places the concept of sexuality at its core to examine citizenship, education, reproduction, science, tourism, urban/rural space, and politics. Topics may include: gender, race, identities, power, transformation, reproduction. Same as SOC 202.</description><creditHours>3 hours.</creditHours><courseSectionInformation>Same as SOC 202.</courseSectionInformation><sectionDegreeAttributes>Cultural Studies - Western course.</sectionDegreeAttributes><genEdCategories><category id="CS"><description>Cultural Studies</description><ns2:genEdAttributes><genEdAttribute code="1WCC">Cultural Studies - Western</genEdAttribute></ns2:genEdAttributes></category></genEdCategories><sections><section id="61621" href="schedule/2022/spring/GWS/202/61621.xml">AD1</section><section id="61628" href="schedule/2022/spring/GWS/202/61628.xml">AD2</section><section id="61631" href="schedule/2022/spring/GWS/202/61631.xml">AD3</section><section id="61633" href="schedule/2022/spring/GWS/202/61633.xml">AD4</section><section id="71815" href="schedule/2022/spring/GWS/202/71815.xml">AD5</section><section id="71816" href="schedule/2022/spring/GWS/202/71816.xml">AD6</section><section id="61611" href="schedule/2022/spring/GWS/202/61611.xml">AL1</section></sections></ns2:course>